From 5600117fcd16a044e1890d3fe5c0a378b3a9f261 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ravindra Lakkireddy <85186928+rlakki08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 00:12:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] catalog: gaze focus (GET
 /catalog?focus=roof|wall|ground|ceiling|counter|opening)

The app sends what the wearer looks at; per setting (exterior / kitchen / room)
and focus a curated table leads (catalog_tables.FOCUS_TABLES): on a roof solar
panels, gutters, roof vents...; on a wall wall-mounted HVAC, windows, window AC...
Grok's site extras follow where their words put them (Zabel's Red Tile Roofs on
the roof). Stocked categories first; only the first 6 thin ones are searched in
the background. No focus / an unknown one: today's list. Response: focus, foci.

New categories: wall-hvac, wall-vents, downspouts (gutters no longer take the
word), snow-guards, satellite-mounts, pavers, drainage, backsplash.
warm --catalog also fills each site's focus variants (--no-focus,
--max-searches N).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
